  "Question": "The logarithm of \\(0.0625\\) to the base \\(2\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0.025\\)",
    "B": "\\(0.25\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(-4\\)",
    "E": "\\(-2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The base-\\(2\\) logarithm asks which exponent of \\(2\\) produces \\(0.0625\\). Rewrite the decimal as a power of \\(2\\):\n\\[\n0.0625=\\frac{625}{10000}\n=\\frac1{16}=\\frac1{2^4}=2^{-4}.\n\\]\nTherefore \\(\\log_2(0.0625)=-4\\), choice D.",
